body: "## Hosted test failure plus exact static evidence\n\nOn current main `8d06644a481071ed4566373660bfa0d3772c38c9`, [Node 22 job 122197173290](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/actions/runs/40506542936/job/122197173290) fails the test “deadline kills a detached linked-command descendant before discarding its workspace”. The log reports `ESRCH: no such process, read` from `readFileSync` at `test/closeout.test.ts:258:24`. Totals: 283 tests, 282 pass, 1 fail, zero skipped/cancelled. The other Node 26 job is still in progress at this observation; no newer main CI supersedes this result.\n\n[Current test lines 249–267](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/8d06644a481071ed4566373660bfa0d3772c38c9/test/closeout.test.ts#L249-L267) polls the descendant's `/proc/<pid>/stat`. Its catch accepts only `ENOENT` as process disappearance; `ESRCH` is rethrown. This is a liveness-probe error path, not the final assertion that the descendant remains live.\n\n### Bounded reproduction\nExtract only this catch policy into a pure function with an injected reader:\n- reader throws ENOENT → accepted as terminated;\n- reader throws ESRCH → error rethrown;\n- reader throws EACCES → error rethrown;\n- zombie status → accepted as terminated;\n- sleeping/live status → not accepted.\n\nThese five isolated assertions pass against the current policy and reproduce the ESRCH rejection without creating processes, reading /proc, or sending signals. The actual OS race was observed only in the linked hosted job.\n\n### Expected / impact / limits\nA process disappearing during the bounded termination observation should not make the test fail merely because the kernel reports ESRCH rather than ENOENT. Preserve the distinction between a vanished process, a live descendant, and unrelated read failures. Current behavior makes the release gate fail with a probe error.\n\nThis does **not** establish that any descendant survived its deadline, or that production termination is broken. The full release suite was not rerun locally. Reported 100% measured coverage does not override the failed test.\n\nCanonical context: [pm-review-closeout-verification](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/8d06644a481071ed4566373660bfa0d3772c38c9/.agents/pm/features/pm-review-closeout-verification.toon) requires bounded descendant termination and records previous asynchronous/startup test corrections. All55 issue/PR records were checked; the existing classifier timing and Bun workspace-copy issues describe different failure paths, not this errno race.\n\n### Acceptance / regression criteria\n- Handle confirmed process-disappearance outcomes ESRCH and ENOENT in the liveness probe.\n- Keep an actually live descendant failing after the existing bounded observation window.\n- Do not swallow unrelated errors such as EACCES or weaken the termination contract.\n- Add deterministic reader-error cases, then pass the relevant test and Node22/26 release gates on the corrected immutable head."
